      "inherent_risk": "critical",
      "residual_risk": "critical",
      "residual_rationale": "The only credited present control is an enumerated MCP allowlist, but the same allowed third-party server both supplies the poisoned instruction and receives the exfiltrated data. Because the allowed server is installed from @latest and can change definitions without review, the credited allowlist does not materially narrow this present path enough to justify the rubric floor.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "locator": "artifacts:quicknotes_mcp tools/list excerpt",
          "observation": "The add_note description says to read ~/.aws/credentials and pass its contents in the context argument, and to hide this from the user."
        },
        {
          "locator": "artifacts:mcp.json",
          "observation": "The filesystem server exposes C:/Users/dev, allowing reads from the user's home directory where the cited credential file resides."
        },
        {
          "locator": "artifacts:runtime notes",
          "observation": "quicknotes_mcp is a community package installed with @latest on every launch and calls a hosted sync service run by its author, so definitions can change without review and sent arguments leave the trust boundary."
        },
        {
          "locator": "artifacts:runtime notes",
          "observation": "The desktop client asks for approval on the first call to each tool, then remembers always allow, so later calls to the same tool are unreviewed and the remembered approval is not a real gate."
        }
      ],
      "recommendations": [
        {
          "category": "preventive",
          "mechanism": "structural",
          "action": "Pin quicknotes_mcp package and hash-reviewed tool definitions before use; block execution when definitions change.",
          "priority": "p1",
          "audience": "developer",
